<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan CPC adjusts petrochemical prices.</title>
<headline>Taiwan CPC adjusts petrochemical prices.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp said it had adjusted product prices for April.</p>
<p>The prices, annouced at the end of each month, apply retroactively to products sold during the month. (in U.S. dollars per tonne)</p>
<p>PRODUCT					  April	 March</p>
<p>Ethylene					   577	   569</p>
<p>Polymer grade propylene			501	   453</p>
<p>Chemical grade propylene		     468	   420</p>
<p>Butadiene					  425	   425</p>
<p>Benzene					    327	   305</p>
<p>Paraxylene					 479	   452</p>
<p>Orthoxylene					416	   412</p>
<p>Carbon black feedstock (per kilolitre)   107	   101</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
